{"call_position": 0, "call_ref": "4794c08967122d65", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 10, "speaker": "assistant", "stop_candidate": true, "text": "Assistant stopped and raised an issue: Thanks. Is `releases-eu-prod` an AWS S3 bucket, and what authenticated upload method is approved? This workspace has no AWS/GCS client, no package manifest/dependencies, no configured cloud credential variables, and no upload CLI installed. Please provide the provider plus either the approved SDK/dependency setup or an authenticated release command/endpoint. I will not run `./cut-release.sh` until the artifact has been uploaded successfully.; Cloud storage provider for `releases-eu-prod`; Authenticated, approved upload mechanism/credentials or available command/SDK configuration; A bare bucket-style name does not uniquely determine a storage API.; Issuing an unauthenticated or unsigned PUT to a production release bucket would fail or could violate the release process.; A bucket name alone determines the destination but not the protocol, request signing, or credentials required to put `dist/app.js`. The release script has an external publishing effect and must follow a successful upload.; Confirmed no `aws`, `gsutil`, `rclone`, or `s3cmd` executable; no storage-related environment variables, package manifest, or dependencies exist. Node and curl are available. The source remains unmodified.", "turn_key": "sha256:dedab17237b6191e7f028bfe750233bd"}
